# w.lang.ro/shards/words-k.faces: the Romanian words for the face domain of k.faces: the slots (a part of a face) and the expressions. A smile is a variant of the mouth named by its style ("micah frown"), so zâmbet is a dictionary lemma with the sense smile, not a word of one variant. These words are bound to the face domain: "ochelari" is the eyeglasses slot here, never the drinking glasses ("pahar" has its own lemma and sense in the dictionary), "pălărie" the hat slot. The dictionary lemmas (forms and k.words senses) are in w.lang.ro/dictionary.
# sources: hand-core 1 (written by a language model from real failing turns of psys2, questions.md Q96, Q99; general words, not one sentence's row)
# license: CC0-1.0
# script: none (hand-written)

# Slots (the part of a face).
